-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|Install OpenWrt (generic explanation)]]

OpenWrt main (formerly master) images can be installed via the stock firmware on this router using the ''factory'' image file. The unencrypted file for the [[docs:guide-user:installation:installation_methods:d-link_recovery_gui|recovery interface]] is now named ''recovery''.

OpenWrt 23.05 and older <color #ed1c24>**cannot**</color> be installed through the stock firmware on this router, as it only accepts properly signed and encrypted files in D-Link SHRS format. Use the [[docs:guide-user:installation:installation_methods:d-link_recovery_gui|D-Link Recovery GUI]] instead to upload the OpenWrt factory image for this router. 

If the upload from the Recovery GUI hangs and doesn't do anything, refer to [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/d-link-recovery-mode-dir-882-dir-878-dir-867/78758|this forum topic]] for an alternative exploit that can be used in older versions of the stock firmware to get OpenWrt installed.

